# Panel Art
#>panel_art
#:surface #!draft

^"purpose"{
  what: "The book's places, characters and tropes as drawings any page can show, so a new scene costs a record and not a commission."
  code: ~"book/scripts/modules/panel-art.mjs"
  figures: ~"book/scripts/modules/characters.mjs"
}

^"composition"{
  source: "The maker's laminated panels, public at spwashi.com/design/folios. What carries over is how a panel is put together. No scan or caption is copied into this tree."
  wash: "long dry strokes at one lean, roughened"
  horizon: "a terraced edge, two layers, a stair and not a slope"
  disc: "one or a pair, standing over the horizon, shaded off centre"
  ink: "thin cream line laid on top of the paint"
  palette: "plum, maroon, violet and storm grounds; teal and amber lit from within, per the boonberry form"
}

^"vocabulary"[
  { kind: "place", where: "PLACES in panel-art.mjs", cost: "a palette, a horizon, discs and one ink" }
  { kind: "figure", where: "STAND in characters.mjs", cost: "one drawing, feet at y 100" }
  { kind: "mood", where: "mien() in each portrait", cost: "a face per mood; the figure in plain lines has none" }
  { kind: "emblem", where: "PROPS in panel-art.mjs", cost: "one prop on a 64 tile, keyed to a trope id" }
]

!guards[
  "nobody in a panel speaks"
  "the figure in plain lines stays one circle, one rectangle, four lines and two dots at any scale, and the hat rests above and never lands"
  "children are never drawn, and no stranger is placed among them"
  "every id inside an SVG is prefixed, so panels can share a document"
]

?open[
  "The six places are the game's. The 71 chapter scene blocks have vantage, light and edges that could each pick a ground and an ink. Whether a scene block should draw itself is the author's call."
  "Cast in a panel is chosen by hand here. Who may stand with whom should follow way.json once a pairing has been read in its paragraph."
]
